# Component Validation

## File Purpose and Relationship

This file defines the process for validating React components within the front-end workflow. It should be consulted when:

- Verifying that component implementations meet established standards
- Ensuring components follow best practices for performance and maintainability
- Checking for proper type definitions and prop handling
- Confirming accessibility compliance
- Verifying test coverage

This file complements:
- **hook-validation.md**: Hook implementation validation
- **state-validation.md**: State management validation
- **component-finalization.md**: Component finalization process
- **fix-component-issues.md**: Component issue resolution

## Usage as Project-Rule-Parameter

This file contains the validation process for React components and should be referenced as a project-rule-parameter when comprehensive component validation is needed:

```
validate-component: front-end/src/components/ComponentName.tsx @parameters/front-end/helpers/validation/component-validation.mdc
```

## Command Format

```
validate-component: [component-path] @parameters/front-end/helpers/validation/component-validation.mdc
```

## Required Context

To perform component validation, the following context is required:

1. Access to the component source file
2. Access to the component test file(s)
3. Understanding of the component's purpose and requirements
4. Knowledge of React best practices and established patterns

## Process Steps

### 1. Component Structure Validation

First, validate the basic structure of the component:

```typescript
// Read the component file
read_file("front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Check component definition pattern
grep_search("export (const|function) [A-Za-z]+( *=|:| =) *(React\\.)?FC<", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check proper exports
grep_search("export default [A-Za-z]+;", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")
```

### 2. Type Safety Verification

Verify type safety and proper type definitions:

```typescript
// Check for props interface
grep_search("interface [A-Za-z]+Props", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for proper typing
grep_search(": React\\.FC<[A-Za-z]+Props>", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for prop destructuring
grep_search("const \\{ [a-zA-Z0-9_, ]+ \\} = props", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")
```

### 3. Performance Optimization Validation

Check for performance optimizations:

```typescript
// Check for memoization
grep_search("React\\.memo|memo\\(|useMemo|useCallback", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for dependency arrays
grep_search("\\[\\]\\)|\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\)", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for unnecessary re-renders
grep_search("useEffect\\(\\(\\) => \\{[^\\}]+\\}, \\[\\]\\)", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")
```

### 4. Accessibility Validation

Validate accessibility features:

```typescript
// Check for semantic HTML
grep_search("<(header|main|footer|nav|section|article|aside)>", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for accessibility attributes
grep_search("aria-|role=", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for alt text on images
grep_search("<img [^>]*alt=", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")
```

### 5. Test Coverage Verification

Verify test coverage for the component:

```typescript
// Read test file
read_file("front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.test.tsx", should_read_entire_file=true)

// Check for proper test setup
grep_search("import |render|screen|fireEvent|waitFor|act", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.test.tsx")

// Check test coverage
grep_search("test\\(|it\\(|describe\\(", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.test.tsx")

// Check assertions
grep_search("expect\\(", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.test.tsx")
```

### 6. Error Handling Validation

Check for proper error handling:

```typescript
// Check for error states
grep_search("(error|Error|isError)", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for loading states
grep_search("(loading|Loading|isLoading)", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")

// Check for try/catch blocks
grep_search("try {[^}]+} catch", false, "front-end/src/components/ExampleComponent/ExampleComponent.tsx")
```

## Expected Outputs

The validation process should produce:

1. A component validation report
2. A list of any standards or best practices not followed
3. Recommendations for improvements
4. Validation status (Pass/Fail/Partial)

## Error Handling

Common component issues and their resolutions:

| Issue | Resolution |
|-------|------------|
| Missing type definitions | Add proper interface for props |
| No performance optimizations | Implement React.memo or useMemo where appropriate |
| Accessibility issues | Add proper aria attributes and semantic HTML |
| Insufficient test coverage | Add tests for all component behaviors |
| No error handling | Implement proper error states and handling |
| Improper prop handling | Use prop destructuring and defaultProps |

## Validation Report Creation

Create a comprehensive validation report:

```typescript
// Create validation report
edit_file("validation-reports/ExampleComponent-validation.md",
          "Create component validation report",
          "# Component Validation: ExampleComponent\n\n## Structure Validation\n- Component Definition: ✅\n- Proper Exports: ✅\n- File Organization: ✅\n\n## Type Safety\n- Props Interface: ✅\n- Proper Typing: ✅\n- Prop Destructuring: ✅\n\n## Performance Optimization\n- Memoization: ❌\n- Dependency Arrays: ✅\n- Render Optimization: ⚠️\n\n## Accessibility\n- Semantic HTML: ✅\n- ARIA Attributes: ❌\n- Alt Text: ✅\n\n## Test Coverage\n- Unit Tests: ✅\n- Integration Tests: ❌\n- Edge Cases: ⚠️\n\n## Error Handling\n- Error States: ✅\n- Loading States: ✅\n- Try/Catch Blocks: ❌\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. Add React.memo to prevent unnecessary re-renders\n2. Add aria-label attributes to interactive elements\n3. Add integration tests for component\n4. Implement proper try/catch blocks for async operations\n\n## Validation Status\n\nPartial Pass - Improvements needed in accessibility and error handling")
```

## Automated Component Validation

For more efficient validation of multiple components, the following tool sequence can be used:

```typescript
// 1. Get list of components
run_terminal_cmd("Get-ChildItem -Path 'front-end/src/components' -Directory | ForEach-Object { $_.Name }", false, false)

// 2. Loop through components and validate
// Note: This would be implemented in a script, shown here for reference
run_terminal_cmd("foreach ($component in (Get-ChildItem -Path 'front-end/src/components' -Directory)) { Write-Output \"Validating $($component.Name)...\" }", false, false)

// 3. Create consolidated report
edit_file("front-end/validation-reports/component-validation-summary.md",
          "Create component validation summary",
          "# Component Validation Summary\n\n## Overview\n\n| Component | Structure | Type Safety | Performance | Accessibility | Test Coverage | Error Handling | Status |\n|-----------|-----------|------------|------------|--------------|--------------|---------------|--------|\n| Button | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | Pass |\n| Card | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ | ✅ | ✅ | ⚠️ | Partial |\n| Modal | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ | ⚠️ | ❌ | Fail |\n\n## Recommendations Summary\n\n- Add memoization to 3 components\n- Improve accessibility in 2 components\n- Enhance test coverage for 4 components\n- Add error handling to 5 components")
```

This validation process ensures that React components adhere to established standards, follow best practices, and maintain high quality throughout the front-end codebase. 